---
import {
  firstDistroUrl,
  getSocialLink,
  sinchUrl,
  siteEmail,
  useLayUrl,
  wonderstandUrl,
} from '@shared/lib/site'

const x = getSocialLink('X')
const github = getSocialLink('GitHub')
---

<section class="home-letter" aria-label="Introduction">
  <h1>I'm Jide, a product design engineer.</h1>
  <p>I founded these, and I still design and build them.</p>
  <p>
    <a href={wonderstandUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
      Wonderstand
      <span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span>
    </a>{' '}
    is the realtor OS. From iMessage, SMS, and WhatsApp, AI agents answer
    buyers, and realtors send them to handle customers, listings, and
    contracts.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href={firstDistroUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
      FirstDistro
      <span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span>
    </a>{' '}
    is account intelligence for customer success.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href={useLayUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
      UseLay
      <span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span>
    </a>{' '}
    is in-app feedback that pins comments to the UI.
  </p>
  <p class="home-letter__job">
    Dayside I'm a senior product designer at{' '}
    <a href={sinchUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
      Sinch
      <span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span>
    </a>
    , on messaging and AI for businesses. Off hours: local models.
  </p>
  <p>
    Reach me on{' '}
    <a href={x.href} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
      X
      <span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span>
    </a>
    ,{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${siteEmail}`}>email</a>
    , or{' '}
    <a href={github.href} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
      GitHub
      <span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span>
    </a>
    .
  </p>
</section>
